  <hazard>- Incompatible codes and drawstrings 
- Part: ① Drawstring, ② Hood drawstring, ③ Non-fixed toggle
- Measured value: ① Not bartacked
② Drawstring present in head area of infant clothing (ages 3 to 7)
③ No protruding loops, but toggle is not fixed to the garment.
- Standard limit: ① If a drawstring is used, it must be bartacked and attached to the clothing at least at one point equidistant from the exit point 
② Infant clothing must not have drawstrings or functional cords in the head, neck, or upper chest areas
③ For clothing without free-end drawstrings, there should be no protruding loops when the garment is laid flat with the opening maximized, and the toggle used to adjust the free-end drawstring must be fixed to the garment
- Inadequate labeling
- Omission of fiber composition (English only), manufacturer''s or importer''s name
- Risk of accidents due to entrapment or entanglement of cords and drawstrings</hazard>
  <injuries>No injury has been reported</injuries>
  <action>- Consumers possessing the affected product must cease use immediately.
